  <h1 class="mb-5 mt-0 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight text-base-content sm:text-[2.8rem]">State Availability</h1>

  <div class="answer-first">
    <span class="af-label">In short</span>
    <p><strong>This site blocks commercial offers in 14 states:</strong> {% for s in collections.closedStates %}{{ s.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. This is our offer-blocking policy, not a verified list of states where every sweepstakes casino is illegal.</p>
    <p>Site policy, operator restrictions and legal status are separate questions. All research remains public. The table below covers all 50 states and DC; a state without a site-wide block is not legal clearance or confirmation that an operator accepts you.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>How the gate works on this site</h2>
  <p>Select your state below. Your choice is stored on your device for 30 days and controls only whether affiliate links are displayed; it never changes which articles you can read.</p>

  <section class="eligibility" aria-label="State selection">
    <h2>Your state</h2>
    <p>Stored locally for 30 days. Nothing is sent to us.</p>
    <div class="js-only">
      <label for="state-picker" class="mb-1.5 block text-sm font-semibold text-base-content/60">State</label>
      <select id="state-picker" data-state-picker>
        {% for s in states %}<option value="{{ s.code }}"{% if not s.code %} disabled selected{% endif %}>{{ s.name }}</option>{% endfor %}
      </select>
      <p class="eligibility-note">Current selection: <strong data-state-echo>not selected</strong>.</p>
    </div>
    <noscript><p class="eligibility-note">State selection requires JavaScript.</p></noscript>
  </section>

  <h2 id="closed-states">State-by-state offer policy</h2>
  <p>Page updated September 18, 2026. Existing gate settings are unchanged. State records link to operator evidence and identify where legal-source review is still incomplete.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table class="data">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">Site offer policy</th><th scope="col">Legal-source coverage</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{% for s in states %}{% if s.code %}
      <tr id="state-{{ s.code | lower }}"><th scope="row">{% if s.slug %}<a href="/availability/{{ s.slug }}/">{{ s.name }}</a>{% else %}{{ s.name }}{% endif %}</th>
      <td>{% if s.status == "statute" or s.status == "enforcement" %}Offers blocked{% else %}No site-wide block; operator restrictions still apply{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{% if stateEvidence[s.code] %}<a href="/availability/{{ s.slug }}/#legal-sources">Primary-source note available</a>{% else %}State-specific legal review not completed{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}</tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2 id="legal-sources">Legal sources and limits</h2>
  {% for code, evidence in stateEvidence %}
  <p>{{ evidence.summary }} <a href="{{ evidence.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ evidence.label }}</a>. Reviewed {{ evidence.reviewedAt | readableDate }}.</p>
  {% endfor %}
  <h2 id="why-legal">Does availability mean legal?</h2>
  <p>No. An operator accepting a state does not establish that its product complies with state law. Promotional sweepstakes, dual-currency casino-style products and entertainment-only games cannot be treated as one legal category. This page does not provide a definitive legal-state list or identify the most recent state closure.</p>
  <h2 id="california-texas">California and Texas</h2>
  <p>California has the specific AB 831 source note above and a <a href="/availability/california/">state record</a>. This site has no state-wide Texas offer block, but we have not completed a Texas legal-source review. That difference in site policy is not a conclusion that the same product is legal in Texas.</p>

  <h2>Not legal advice</h2>
  <p>This page is general information for readers. Confirm the current rules for your state before you play, and speak to a licensed attorney about your own situation.</p>
